0,Mawé language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mawé_language,"The Mawé language of Brazil, also known as Sateré (Mabue, Maragua, Andira, Arapium), is one of the Tupian languages. It is spoken by 7,000 Mawé people, many of them monolingual.",Sateré-Mawé,Tupian
